      "title": "Building and operating an AI application",
      "question": "How do all the pieces fit together?",
      "explanation": "An AI app combines a user interface, application logic, model access, data retrieval, tools and operational controls. Using a hosted foundation model is different from training one. Production engineering must handle secrets, permissions, privacy, retries, monitoring and versioned content.",
      "mechanics": "Client -> authenticated backend -> policy/context layer -> model gateway -> approved tools/retrieval -> validation -> user response. Store source-grounded curriculum in a content system; keep generation, learner records and secrets in separate controlled services.",
      "misconception": "An API key must not be shipped in client-side code. A prototype is not production-ready because one demo worked.",
